Permission for review

You may view and download the covered materials, make private copies, and build
and run those copies locally for the sole purpose of evaluating the code or
conducting a security review. You may make private modifications as needed for
that evaluation or review. This permission applies to paid and unpaid
independent reviewers and security auditors.

You may publish your independent review, audit conclusions, and security
findings without asking for approval or signing a confidentiality agreement.
You may reproduce brief excerpts of covered source code only to the extent
reasonably necessary to explain your analysis. Please avoid publishing secrets,
personal data, or exploitable details before responsible disclosure when
appropriate. The reporting guidance in SECURITY.md describes a private channel;
using it does not impose a gag obligation or prevent lawful reporting.

